---
quiet: true
timeout: 150
---
let $t0 = now()
// The tetragon-scale throughput harness for the flood node's attest
// leg (the detection-throughput precedent, on the flood's own class):
// the archive rule sees the 5-minute compaction pass, and the flood's
// measured peak drain is 800 ev/s — 240k records per worst-case pass,
// 720k for a full 15-minute window. This harness keeps the permanent
// probe at detection-throughput's 100k scale so the suite stays
// load-stable (a 250k run took ~20s standalone and starved sibling
// tests past their timeouts under the runner's parallel jobs); the
// tetragon-scale probes were measured one-off and recorded honestly in
// the clickhouse README's attestation section — 250k (the peak-drain
// 5-minute pass) in ~20s standalone, 750k (the full 15-minute window)
// in ~5.5-6 min. 100k tetragon records here (5 export fixtures x
// repeat 20000, mapped + derived + cast to the stored shape) through
// the archive rule's exact stamping sequence — the uid mint, the
// (time, uid) sort, the stream-mode attest (record fingerprint +
// chain link). The fixtures share 6 distinct timestamps, so the sort
// sees tie buckets of ~20k records broken by uid alone — the
// sort-adversarial shape, heavier than production (tetragon stamps
// carry nanosecond-precision times; live ties are rare). The baseline
// pins the COUNTS (100k records, 100k stamped); the assert at the end
// is a throughput floor: this run measured ~7s wall for the pipeline
// on an M-series laptop (100k records / ~7s ~= 14k records/s end to
// end; the attest marginal is ~11us/record over the sort-only
// baseline, the sort dominates at flood scale — the honest numbers
// live in the clickhouse README's attestation section), and the floor
// leaves 14x headroom so CI load cannot flake it. A regression that
// pushes the leg under 1k records/s fails the assert and the baseline
// records the warning. Re-measure honestly with:
//   TENZIR_INPUT=... uvx tenzir@6.19.1 -f <this file> # time it
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
this = {tetragon: this}
homelab::tetragon::ocsf::map tetragon, ocsf
this = move ocsf
ocsf_derive
ocsf_cast
where class_uid in [ocsf_class_uid("Process Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("File System Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("Network Activity")]
repeat 20000
// The archive leg, verbatim (nodes/tetragon/pipelines/ocsf-archive.tql).
metadata.uid = uuid() if metadata.uid? == null
sort time, metadata.uid
homelab::record_integrity::attest authority_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  chain_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  genesis=false,
  chain="stream"
summarize records = count(), stamped = sum(1 if attestation_list[0]?.fingerprint?.value? != null else 0)
assert (now() - $t0) < 100s, message="tetragon attest leg under throughput floor: 100k records took over 100s (re-measure and re-check the archive pass sizing math)"
